BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup|June
  9 - Visual AI in Healthcare: Ground Truth in the Foundation-Model Era|Onl
 ine
DTSTART:20260609T100000
CATEGORIES:ai,data,frontend
DESCRIPTION:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\
 nLearn how to handle expert label disagreement and build high performing f
 ine-tuned medical foundation models for clinical imaging tasks.\n\n**Date\
 , Time and Location**\n\nJun 09\, 2026\n9:00 AM – 10:30 AM PST\n**[Onlin
 e. Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/events/visual-ai-in-healthc
 are-ground-truth-in-the-foundation-model-era-june-9-2026)**\n\nMedical ima
 ging teams are increasingly fine-tuning foundation models like UNI\, MedSA
 M2\, and BiomedCLIP on small in-house datasets. At that scale\, label disa
 greement is a dominant cause of model failures\, and the disputed ground t
 ruth is what regulators will ask you to defend. We'll build a medical imag
 ing dataset in [FiftyOne](https://docs.voxel51.com/)\, surfacing and analy
 zing the cases where reviewers disagree. From there\, we'll fine-tune a fo
 undation model on cleaned data and use FiftyOne to evaluate where our mode
 l succeeds and fails\, and which data is needed to move the model’s perf
 ormance forward.\n\n**You’ll learn how to:**\n\n* Build a medical imagin
 g dataset that preserves multiple expert annotations as first-class fields
 \n* Use FiftyOne views\, embedding similarity\, and confidence-disagreemen
 t signals to find the samples where reviewers split.\n* Run label-quality 
 screens\, near-duplicate detection\, and active-learning sample selection 
 using foundation model embeddings\n* Fine-tune a medical foundation model 
 on a defensible dataset\, with auditable and versioned experiment tracking
 \n* Filter and slice evaluation for regulatory and clinical readiness\n* D
 rive the pipeline with natural-language agents using the FiftyOne MCP Serv
 er and Skills to run the same curation\, evaluation\, and review workflows
  from your favorite AI tool\n\n**Who This Is For**\n\n* ML and computer-vi
 sion engineers in the medical imaging space\n* Data and annotation operati
 ons teams\n* Clinical AI and digital pathology leads\n* Regulatory and qua
 lity leads
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Agility Talks|Evolución de Prácticas de Entrega Continua en tiem
 pos de IA|Online
DTSTART:20260616T183000
CATEGORIES:frontend
DESCRIPTION:Agile Talks - Difundiendo la agilidad\n**Evolución de Prácti
 cas de Entrega Continua en tiempos de Desarrollo de software con IA**\n\nL
 a entrega continua de software sigue siendo el modo de máximo flujo de va
 lor para el negocio en desarrollo de software\, a pesar de que a muchas or
 ganizaciones todavía les cueste implementar muchas de sus prácticas cent
 rales\, como integración continua\, automatización de pruebas de aceptac
 ión y entregas frecuentes.\nAl mismo tiempo\, el cambio acelerado en la c
 apacidad de producir software utilizando prácticas y herramientas de IA p
 one en discusión qué cambia\, y qué sigue siendo igual\, en nuestras pr
 ácticas y procesos. El balance entre responsabilidad\, capacidad y calida
 d nos desafía a explorar nuevas formas de desarrollar mientras mantenemos
  los avances que hemos logrado. En este contexto de incertidumbre\, nos en
 contramos para compartir preguntas\, experiencias y algunas de las respues
 tas que están emergiendo.\n\n**Patrocinado por ScrumAlliance.**\n\n**Dieg
 o Fontdevila** es consultor\, profesor e investigador con una trayectoria 
 centrada en elevar el nivel de la práctica en la comunidad de desarrollo 
 de software. A lo largo de su carrera\, ha trabajado impulsando enfoques q
 ue combinan agilidad y excelencia técnica\, convencido de que la agilidad
  sin una base sólida es solo una ilusión.\nPara Diego\, la calidad no es
  un lujo\, sino un principio fundamental para garantizar la continuidad de
 l negocio y la sostenibilidad de las organizaciones.\nForma parte de Grupo
  Esfera\, donde desde hace más de 20 años colaboran con líderes de TI y
  CTOs en procesos de transformación organizacional\, apoyándose no en so
 luciones mágicas\, sino en un enfoque estructurado y probado: el **Esfera
  Way**.
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup|June
  17 - How to Build Vision Data Agents with Tools\, Skills\, and MCP Worksh
 op|Online
DTSTART:20260617T100000
CATEGORIES:ai,backend,data,frontend
DESCRIPTION:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\
 nIn this session\, you’ll learn how to build production-ready AI agents 
 that can reason over your data\, automate complex tasks\, and integrate se
 amlessly into your existing stack using tools\, skills\, and the Model Con
 text Protocol (MCP).\n\n**Time\, Date and Location**\n\nJun 17\, 2026\n9 A
 M Pacific\nOnline. **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/events/h
 ow-to-build-vision-data-agents-with-tools-skills-and-mcp-june-17-2026)**\n
 \nAI agents are rapidly changing how teams build and scale machine learnin
 g workflows—but most implementations still rely on fragmented tools\, ma
 nual processes\, and brittle integrations.\n\nWe’ll walk through how mod
 ern agentic systems move beyond simple prompts—leveraging structured too
 ls like dataset operations\, embeddings\, evaluation pipelines\, and model
  execution to take real action. You’ll see how these agents can tag data
 \, run inference\, evaluate performance\, and surface insights automatical
 ly\, all within a unified workflow.\n\nBy combining natural language inter
 faces with programmable building blocks\, teams can dramatically reduce ma
 nual effort\, accelerate experimentation\, and unlock faster decision-maki
 ng across the ML lifecycle.\n\nWhether you're building data-centric AI sys
 tems\, managing large-scale vision datasets\, or exploring agentic workflo
 ws for the first time\, this session will give you a practical blueprint f
 or getting started.\n\nWhat you’ll learn:\n\n* **How AI agents actually 
 work in production:** Move beyond hype—understand how agents use tools\,
  memory\, and structured workflows to execute real tasks\n* **Using tools 
 to take action on your data:** Program agents to run operations like filte
 ring labels\, computing embeddings\, evaluating detections\, and more\n* *
 *What “skills” are and how they enable multi-step workflows:** Learn h
 ow to package complex logic into reusable capabilities your agents can cal
 l on demand\n* **How MCP connects your models\, tools\, and agents:** See 
 how MCP standardizes communication between LLMs and external systems for s
 calable\, flexible architectures\n* **Automating the ML lifecycle with age
 nts:** From data curation to model evaluation\, discover how to eliminate 
 repetitive workflows and accelerate iteration\n* **Best practices for buil
 ding reliable agentic systems:** Design patterns\, guardrails\, and practi
 cal tips for deploying agents in real-world environments
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
